#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:15
msgid "unzipper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:17
msgid ""
"This is an active fork and drop-in replacement of the [node-"
"unzip](https://github.com/EvanOxfeld/node-unzip) and addresses the "
"following issues:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:18
msgid ""
"finish/close events are not always triggered, particular when the input "
"stream is slower than the receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:19
msgid "Any files are buffered into memory before passing on to entry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:21
msgid ""
"The structure of this fork is similar to the original, but uses Promises "
"and inherit guarantees provided by node streams to ensure low memory "
"footprint and emits finish/close events at the end of processing.   The "
"new `Parser` will push any parsed `entries` downstream if you pipe from "
"it, while still supporting the legacy `entry` event as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:23
msgid ""
"Breaking changes: The new `Parser` will not automatically drain entries "
"if there are no listeners or pipes in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:25
msgid ""
"Unzipper provides simple APIs similar to [node-"
"tar](https://github.com/isaacs/node-tar) for parsing and extracting zip "
"files. There are no added compiled dependencies - inflation is handled by"
" node.js's built in zlib support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:28
msgid ""
"Please note:  Methods that use the Central Directory instead of parsing "
"entire file can be found under [`Open`](#open)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/unzipper_README.md:30
msgid ""
"Chrome extension files (.crx) are zipfiles with an [extra "
"header](http://www.adambarth.com/experimental/crx/docs/crx.html) at the "
"start of the file.  Unzipper will parse .crx file with the streaming "
"methods (`Parse` and `ParseOne`).  The `Open` methods will check for "
"`crx` headers and parse crx files, but only if you provide `crx: true` in"
" options."
msgstr ""

